Subject: Fix ambiguous fmt::format_to() call under GCC 14 in util/ip_address.h
Filename: dhi-fmt-ambiguous-format-to.patch
DHI definition: package/main/opentelemetry-ebpf-reducer/debian-13/0.yaml (patch@v1)

Not an upstream-known issue (v0.11.0 was never built with GCC 14) and not
tied to a public upstream bug report - found and fixed during DHI packaging.
The fmt::formatter<IPv6Address>::format() specialization calls an unqualified
format_to() that bundled fmt v9 (vendored via spdlog, see
https://github.com/gabime/spdlog/tree/master/include/spdlog/fmt/bundled)
resolves ambiguously under our GCC 14 toolchain (two overloads match equally
well). Worked around with a plain std::copy, since the call's only job is
copying a pre-computed string into the output iterator.

DHI PR: https://github.com/docker-hardened-images/definitions-external/pull/623

diff --git a/util/ip_address.h b/util/ip_address.h
--- a/util/ip_address.h
+++ b/util/ip_address.h
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@

 #include <spdlog/fmt/fmt.h>

+#include <algorithm>
 #include <array>
 #include <iostream>
 #include <netinet/in.h>
@@ -116,7 +117,8 @@

   template <typename FormatContext> auto format(const IPv6Address &p, FormatContext &ctx)
   {
-    return format_to(ctx.out(), "{}", p.str());
+    auto s = p.str();
+    return std::copy(s.begin(), s.end(), ctx.out());
   }
 };
 } // namespace fmt
